              <p className="mt-1">👋 <strong>New subscriber:</strong> the new subscriber gets a welcome credit from the <strong className="text-[var(--text)]">Earning Pool</strong> (the driver earning pool) on their own first paid plan — once per account, ever. The credit is a set dollar value, paid in $STONER at the market price when each part pays out, set by their first paid plan: <strong className="text-[var(--text)]">Gold — ${referralQuery.data.welcomeCreditAmountsUsd.gold.toFixed(2)} · Diamond — ${referralQuery.data.welcomeCreditAmountsUsd.diamond.toFixed(2)} · Fleet — ${referralQuery.data.welcomeCreditAmountsUsd.owner.toFixed(2)}</strong>. Upgrading later never tops it up. Diamond's and Fleet's credits vest instead of landing liquid: 25% at the first subscription, then the rest in 6 monthly parts (Diamond) or 12 monthly parts (Fleet) — vesting continues only while the plan stays active; if the plan doesn't renew, vesting pauses on a 2-week retainer and the unvested remainder returns to the Earning Pool only if the retainer ends un-renewed. Gold's credit is liquid.</p>
